<title>UK: UK natural gas consumption at record level in 1996.</title>
<headline>UK natural gas consumption at record level in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>British natural gas consumption rose to record levels in 1996, the Department of Trade and Industry (DTI) said in a provisional study on Thursday.</p>
<p>The DTI said natural gas consumption soared by 17 percent, mainly due to increased use for electricity generation.</p>
<p>Oil consumption was up by 2.5 percent, while coal consumption was down by 7.5 percent.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7714</p>
